{"name":"Queen Anne","hex":"#fab001","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Queen Anne","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Queen Anne of Great Britain (reigned 1702–1714).","The style of architecture, furniture, etc. popular during the reign of Queen Anne."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Queen_Anne"}],"entries":[{"title":"Anne, Queen of Great Britain","blocks":[{"text":"Anne was Queen of England, Scotland, and Ireland from 8 March 1702, and Queen of Great Britain and Ireland following the ratification of the Acts of Union 1707 merging the kingdoms of England and Scotland, until her death in 1714."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg/330px-Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anne%2C_Queen_of_Great_Britain","wikidata":"Q119702"},{"title":"Queen Anne style architecture","blocks":[{"text":"The Queen Anne style of British architecture refers to either the English Baroque architecture of the time of Queen Anne or the British Queen Anne Revival form that became popular during the last quarter of the 19th century and the early decades of the 20th century. In other English-speaking parts of the world, New World Queen Anne Revival architecture embodies entirely different styles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Winslow_Hall%2C_Sheep_Street%2C_Winslow_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2230591.jpg/330px-Winslow_Hall%2C_Sheep_Street%2C_Winslow_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2230591.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queen_Anne_style_architecture","wikidata":"Q529819"},{"title":"Anne","blocks":[{"text":"Anne, alternatively spelled Ann, is a form of the Latin female name Anna. This in turn is a representation of the Hebrew Hannah, which means 'favour' or 'grace'. Related names include Annie and Ana."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg/330px-Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anne","wikidata":"Q564684"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg/500px-Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg/1280px-Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg/500px-Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnne1705.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/The_Duke_and_Duchess_of_York_with_their_two_daughters..jpg/500px-The_Duke_and_Duchess_of_York_with_their_two_daughters..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/The_Duke_and_Duchess_of_York_with_their_two_daughters..jpg/1280px-The_Duke_and_Duchess_of_York_with_their_two_daughters..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/The_Duke_and_Duchess_of_York_with_their_two_daughters..jpg/500px-The_Duke_and_Duchess_of_York_with_their_two_daughters..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Anne (centre) and her sister Mary (left) with their parents, the Duke and Duchess of York, painted b